llection of remembering that means  that the knowledge is in some way  already within us at least within our  minds or our souls and it's a matter of  bringing to light what we don't quite  realize yet that we already know so this  is an attractive doctrine to quite a few  people and I want to be very clear in  distinguishing this from some new agey  beliefs that seem to say something  similar because Plato sang something  quite different you notice a previous  life and present life up here and plain  one does not have in mind previous life  as you know like a version of the  current life just you know way back then  that's what we call the doctrine of  reincarnation Plato actually does seem  to have believed in or taught a doctrine  of reincarnation where the soul is at  death freed from the body the soul  continues to live and that it is  reincarnated as is put back into another  body but something really important  happens with the soul in these intervals  before it goes into another body that's  what the past life refers to that's what  the memory is going back to so I'm not  remembering my past life as you know the  warrior Trog or something like that that  would be a life within this body this is  happening in a different kind of  existence the world of the forms you're  gonna see this discussed in you know the  Phaedrus discussed in the Phaedo  discussed in a lot of different places  here in the Meno he invokes some of the  the mystery religions and he's giving  his own interpretation of it and he  doesn't flesh it out completely but he  doesn't actually need to he gets across  the main  he wants to do and you know so get this  sort of diagram up here I think this  will help us to wrap our heads around it  so the idea is we're here in this  present life and there's something that  we don't know that we don't understand  and somebody else is teaching us about  it now it is the teacher himself or  herself implanting knowledge into our  soul Plato says no a lot 